{%- comment -%}
  FAQPage structured data for an accordion's question blocks.

  Emitted for one page only. Two pages of the same site carrying FAQPage for
  questions worded the same way compete for the same rich result, so the section
  gates this behind a setting rather than emitting it wherever an accordion
  appears. The homepage carries it; /pages/faq deliberately does not.

  Answers are rich text. Google wants the answer as text or limited HTML, and a
  block-level wrapper is fine, but the JSON has to be valid — so the value is
  passed through `json`, which escapes the quotes and newlines for us rather
  than us trying to.

  Accepts:
  - blocks: {Array} The section's blocks. Only `question` types are read.

  Usage:
  {% render 'hs-schema-faq', blocks: section.blocks %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign questions = blocks | where: 'type', 'question'
  assign answered = ''
  for q in questions
    if q.settings.question != blank and q.settings.answer != blank
      assign answered = answered | append: 'y'
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- if answered != '' -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {%- assign first = true -%}
        {%- for q in questions -%}
          {%- if q.settings.question != blank and q.settings.answer != blank -%}
            {%- unless first %},{% endunless -%}
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": {{ q.settings.question | strip_html | json }},
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": {{ q.settings.answer | json }}
              }
            }
            {%- assign first = false -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ]
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
